.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt OCIFBSD-EXPORT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ocifbsd-export
.Nd ocifbsd cloud export and migration tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
tool exports
.Xr ocifbsd 8
containers and jails to portable formats and re-imports them
on the same or different host.
.Pp
ed formats include:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Flat Export Bundle
.Pq .feb
\(em self-contained single-file archive with metadata,
root filesystem, volumes, and config.
.It
Raw disk image and QCOW2.
.It
Cloud provider images: AWS AMI, GCP image, Azure VHD.
.El
.Pp
The commands are:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm export Ar name
Export container
.Ar name
to a FEB file in
.Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/exports/ .
.It Cm import Ar feb_path Ar target_name
Import a FEB file as container
.Ar target_name .
.It Cm list
List all export jobs.
.It Cm status
Show export module statistics.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/lib/ocifbsd/exports -compact
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/exports
Default FEB export directory.
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/containers
Container root filesystems and configs.
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/volumes
Container volumes.
.It Pa /var/lib/ocifbsd/jails
Jail configurations.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ocifbsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was developed by
.An REVYTECH, Inc.
